$ jailops app install nginx --image freebsd-151@stable --dry-run
Dry run: nothing was created. Installing app nginx as jail nginx would do:
  01 create-jail: create thin jail nginx from freebsd-151@stable
  02 start-jail: start nginx
  03 install-packages-ports: pkg -r <root> install -y nginx
  04 record-version: pkg -r <root> query %v nginx, then label jailops.app.version
  05 write-rc-conf: set the services' rc.conf variables in <root>/etc/rc.conf
  06 start-service-nginx: in the jail: /usr/sbin/service nginx start
  07 health-check: the health check of the definition
  08 close-firewall: firewall policy app-nginx (managed by app access): deny every inbound connection until jailops app allow nginx from SOURCE
  09 snapshot: snapshot every dataset of nginx as app-installed

$ jailops app install nginx --image freebsd-151@stable
App nginx installed as jail nginx (running)
  Version:   1.30.6,3
  Addresses: 10.20.0.10
  Ports:     http 80/tcp at 10.20.0.10:80 (expose: forwarding is not set up yet) HTTP, the default site.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow nginx from SOURCE
  Data:      /usr/local/www The sites.
  Config:    /usr/local/etc/nginx/nginx.conf (restart nginx) The server configuration.
  Logs:      access /var/log/nginx/access.log One line per request.
             error /var/log/nginx/error.log
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback nginx --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     9 done
Notes:
  Put the site under /usr/local/www.

$ jailops app install postgresql --name db --image freebsd-151@stable --network lan --storage default --memory 2G --disk 20G --cpu 2
App postgresql installed as jail db (running)
  Version:   18.6
  Addresses: 10.20.0.11
  Ports:     postgres 5432/tcp at 10.20.0.11:5432 The SQL port.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow db from SOURCE
  Data:      /var/db/postgres The cluster (data18).
  Config:    /var/db/postgres/data18/postgresql.conf (restart postgresql) Server settings.
             /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf (restart postgresql) Who may connect.
  Logs:      server /var/log/messages The port logs to syslog.
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback db --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     11 done
Notes:
  Connect from inside the jail with: jailops exec NAME -- su -l postgres -c psql

